# CyberFlap

Virtual split-flap display web app. Own product — never refer to competing brands in code, comments, UI, or filenames.

## Stack

- Vite + React (JavaScript, not TypeScript)
- React Router: `/` (board), `/settings`
- No backend; persistence via `localStorage`

## Layout (`src/`)

- `components/` — `Board`, `Tile` (+ CSS)
- `content/` — clock, weather, message, rainbow, rotation hooks, `config.js`
- `pages/` — `BoardPage`, `SettingsPage`
- `utils/` — `characters.js`, `board.js`, `useBoard.js`, `flipSound.js`

## Board model

- Fixed **22 columns**; dynamic **1–6 rows** (no empty trailing rows)
- Wrap/truncate via `layoutText()` in `utils/board.js` (`MAX_ROWS = 6`)
- Tile codes in `utils/characters.js`: blank `0`, A–Z `1–26`, digits `27–36` (1–9 then 0), punctuation, colors `63–70`
- Helpers: `tileFromChar`, `tileFromColor`, `getFlipPath`, `FLIP_SEQUENCE`
- Tile size: ~3:2, CSS `clamp` on `--tile-w` (viewport-based, not row-count-based)
- Wider **row-gap** than column-gap; board height CSS-transitions (~260ms) on row count change

## Flip animation

- Each step uses CSS `rotateX` split-flap (top then bottom half), ~72ms (`FLIP_STEP_MS`)
- Walk shortest path on `FLIP_SEQUENCE`; stagger starts per cell
- Only tiles whose codes change should animate (`useBoard` skips equal boards)
- Per flip **step** (not whole tile): `playFlipClick()` from `utils/flipSound.js`

## Content rotation

Order: `clock` → `weather` → `message` (`MODULE_ORDER`). Defaults in `content/config.js` (10s dwell, etc.).

| Module | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| clock | 1-line time with seconds; tick 1s while active |
| weather | Open-Meteo + geolocation (SF fallback); refresh 15m |
| message | Single custom string from `localStorage` |

Manual override shows a sample ~10s then resumes. Playback: Previous / Pause-Resume / Next (Next/Prev reset auto-advance timer).

## Rainbow mode (`cyberflap.rainbowMode`, default on)

- Off or **1 row** → neutral tiles
- **6 rows** → full spectrum, per-color ink OK
- **2–5 rows** → colors from one contrast group so **all rows share one text color**
  - Dark/white ink: red, violet
  - Light/black ink: orange, yellow, green, blue
  - 5 rows: light group + best extra for black ink (red), single black ink

## Settings (`/settings`)

- Custom message + Save → `cyberflap.customMessage`
- Rainbow checkbox (persists immediately)
- Live wrap preview via `getPreviewLines()` (and rainbow preview colors)

## Sound

- Web Audio only (no audio files): ~30ms filtered-noise clack
- Cap concurrent voices / scale gain; unlock `AudioContext` on first user gesture
- Mute: `cyberflap.mute` (default unmuted); toggle next to playback

## Brand / UI

- Wordmark + cyan/magenta/dark-navy look (Orbitron + Share Tech Mono)
- Gear → settings; don’t let chrome overpower the board

## Prompt history (canonical)

1 scaffold → 2 grid/chars → 3 rebrand+flip → 4 content+rotation → 5 dynamic rows → 6 settings route → 7 row gap+rainbow → 8 ink groups+playback → 9 flip sound

When extending: keep board codes/layout central, prefer `localStorage` for prefs, match existing visual language, number future prompts.
